2. Protocol: src/protocol/mod.rs implements the completed protocol ICD;
   protocol.schema.json is generated with schemars. Five JSONL golden fixtures
   cover every item, parallel reads, interruption, recovery, Lagged and Reset.
   src/protocol/laws.rs checks endings, pairing, item/turn ordering and durable
   sequence/epoch order. tests/protocol_golden.rs checks exact wire round trips.
3. Core: src/engine/mod.rs owns work/control queues, op deduplication, pending
   approvals, turn/steer queues and the single store writer. turn_loop.rs uses
   the shared Yarn topology and generation fence; task_group.rs owns and joins
   child tasks. process.rs terminates only its spawned process group, joins
   pipes and reaps the leader. provider/ assembles strict SSE calls, preserves
   opaque reasoning and retries only before output. tools.rs declares effects,
   stages patches, requires exact unique edits, limits parallel reads and locks
   write paths. policy.rs records rules and unattended decisions. store.rs
   recovers innermost items, synthesizes tool results and writes redacted blobs.
   gateway/ supplies InProc and Unix, replay, open-item snapshots, lag and reset.
   frontends/ supplies headless JSONL, cooked seat input and the line projection.
4. Formal: tests/formal/ uses the published native checker, paired broken
   controls and a shared reactor!/reactor_model! declaration. The corpus has 23
   models, one crate and eleven paired contract families. The adapted upstream
   pipeline compares full state/transition sets and native/Java verdicts, pins
   Java/TLC hashes and preserves source-bound evidence locally. These finite
   contracts do not prove arbitrary Rust, real HTTP, filesystem durability,
   kernel timing, or rendering.
5. Live smoke: the requested Nemotron profile/key command and a three-request
